1. Tap the Movement setting on the left side. A Motion Profile field with the following choices appears on the right side. Joint_slow is the default. • Custom • Joint_fast • Joint_slow 8. When Joint_fast and Joint_slow are selected, the OptiMove speed and acceleration are shown. Software Handbook PolyScope X Copyright © 2009–2026 by Universal Robots A/S. All rights reserved. Reference setting In the Frame field, four choices are available: • world • base • flange • tcp In the TCP field, two choices are available: • Active_TCP • Tool_flange 3. In the Position column, tap the X, Y, Z tabs and enter your chosen value for the robot, and Confirm. 4. In the Rotation column, tap the RX, RY, RZ tabs and enter your chosen value for the robot, and Confirm. Transform setting 2. Tap the Pose field and Confirm. PolyScope X Software Handbook Copyright © 2009–2026 by Universal Robots A/S. All rights reserved. Blend setting A Blend type field appears with two options: • Stop at this point • Blend 16.3.16. Linear Move Description The Linear Move command node supports Motions Profiles as Joint Move, but it creates a movement that is a direct line from point A and point B. It moves the Tool Center Point (TCP) linearly between waypoints. This means that each joint performs a more complicated motion to keep the tool on a straight line path. Software Handbook PolyScope X Copyright © 2009–2026 by Universal Robots A/S. All rights reserved. To access Linear Move command 2. Tap the Linear Move icon in the Commands toolbox. A node with two editable fields, two buttons, and ellipsis icon is inserted into the program tree. These are two editable fields: • Motion Profile • Name

